{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3655","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3655","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3655\",\"parent_revision\":\"f0fd20403b00e4d28215e50f8197d201d0c85e67aebe0fab9ce9c3767a9a95c9\",\"root_revision\":\"f0fd20403b00e4d28215e50f8197d201d0c85e67aebe0fab9ce9c3767a9a95c9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring a re-groom, the item's `groomed` field changes to today's date as soon as the orchestrator writes the RT-ICA snapshot in `groom/analyze.md`, before any swarm wave runs and before `finalize.md` calls `mark_groomed=True`.\\n\\nObserved on #3060, 2026-09-19: `groomed` was 2026-08-20 at intake. After `backlog_groom(selector=\\\"#3060\\\", section=\\\"RT-ICA\\\", content=<snapshot>)`, `backlog_view` showed `groomed: 2026-09-19`, while Waves 0-3 and finalize had not run.\\n\\nImpact: `groom/intake.md` Check E (\\\"already groomed today\\\" \u2192 DRIFT) and `work/groom-check.md`'s staleness check both read this field. If a groom stops after the snapshot, a later run reads the item as groomed today and routes to drift instead of re-grooming; the staleness check measures drift from a date on which no grooming finished.\\n\\nExpected: `groomed` changes only when grooming completes (the `mark_groomed=True` write).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, re-groom of #3060, 2026-09-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"43094b1f51e0399580d169a9c90d1e283c99dc422547cc2afd9d9156351dade2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHuSg\"}"}